
# TODO

## Imaging / science features still to implement
- Gaussian fitting (imfit) -> extract beam major/minor/PA, integrated & peak flux,
  residual RMS, fit frequency; log it (from 1.99 auto_gaussian).
- Core subtraction: clean -> copy MS -> uvsub -> re-clean the core-subtracted ("jet")
  image -> pbcor + FITS (from 1.99 core_subtract).
- Outlier fields: generate outliers.txt and feed outlier regions to tclean.
- Off-source RMS box for the self-cal metric. Cleaner._dynamic_range currently uses
  whole-image RMS (contaminated by the source); an off-source annulus/box is more rigorous.
- Optional: drop the .residual.tt0 (as FITS) into the results folder next to image/pbcor.

## Calibration
- Reference antenna: replace "3rd closest by vibes" (find_refant -> anntennas_list[3])
  with a principled central / low-flagging / present-the-whole-track pick, chosen once
  and fixed across cycles. (Array-config detection from antenna layout is done; refant
  selection itself is not.)
- fluxscale-failure retry: when fluxscale fails, try alternate refants with a
  checkpoint backup/restore of the data folder (from 1.99 refant retry loop).
- Manual flux calibration: setjy standard='manual' with user flux/freq, for odd/missing
  amplitude calibrators (Perley-Butler is the only path today).
- "Don't do self phase calibration" toggle.
- Solution bookkeeping: decide & document incremental vs non-incremental self-cal;
  implement check_refant (currently `pass`); optionally save per-cycle gain phase/amp
  plots + stats for archiving.

## Manual self-cal mode
- Flesh out the 'manual_self_cal' breakpoint beyond dropping into a CASA shell: pause to
  let the user inspect the image / gain solutions and choose solint/calmode/continue-or-stop
  per cycle. (Breakpoint routing is fixed; the guided experience is not built.)

## Reproducibility / archiving
- Portable replay bundle: the .mask images that replay.py references live in
  measurement_sets/. Copy the per-cycle masks next to replay.py (or rewrite the paths)
  so a results folder replays on its own.
- Provenance/integrity in import.json: software versions + git commit + input/mask
  checksums (replay.py already carries a provenance header).
- Archiving metadata collection:
  - from user: email, name, reason for reducing; # knots + lobes and notes on the result
  - automatic: calibration problems/statistics, redshift, # of calibration rounds
  - NRAO archive tool: https://data.nrao.edu/archive-service/

## GUI
- Delineate "manual self-cal + cleaning" from interactive cleaning.
- Source-selection GUI: close/submit requires pressing it twice (bug).
- Expanded features.

## Code cleanup / maintainability
- Remove dead stubs: self_cal_solint_variation (duplicate of self_cal_cycle);
  find_solint_variations (image_maker) and phase_self_calibration (main_calibrations)
  are empty and superseded by _build_solint_schedule / self_cal_cycle.
- Turn imstat parsing into an Image-analysis module (classes/image_data.Image is a start).
- Separate user *options* from per-run *data* (hierarchy).
- Remove autopep8, fabric from requirements.
- Excessive-commenting pass.
- Keep example copies of parsed external data (email formats, web-page layouts, casa log
  formatting) for when those formats drift.

### Race conditions
- Split / import don't pause. (plotms now has an accept/revert catch in the flagging
  breakpoint, so that specific race is handled.)

### Testing
- Choose the set of pre-2008 observations to validate against (working ONLY with
  pre-2008 / classic-VLA data -> nterms stays 1, narrow fractional bandwidth).
- listobs format robustness (epoch/srcID columns running together; scan data read-in).

## Possible issues
- Path access when the script is launched from outside the active dir (set cwd at runtime).

## Tech - Exploration
- EC2 web-server endpoint: accept a request, ssh from NRAO -> user as the response (pysocket).
- Import the NRAO calibrator list to auto-fill many more calibrators.


## Recently completed (for reference)
- Self-cal loop rewrite: data-driven solint ladder ('inf' -> geometric halving down to the
  integration time -> 'int', for any n cycles; fixed fallback ladder logged as WARN),
  phase-only cycles + one guarded final amp+phase pass (solnorm), dynamic-range metric,
  keep-best, convergence/divergence early-stop, faint-source flux gate, minsnr, calonly.
- Mode-aware auto-masking (auto-multithresh automatic / nsigma interactive); LAS-bounded
  multiscale scales (fixes multiscale-deconvolver no-op); array config + cell size derived
  from the antenna layout (not a hardcoded config index).
- gaincal failure rate (read from the caltable FLAG column) -> adaptive applymode
  (calflag/calonly) on primary cal + per-cycle self-cal diagnostic.
- Data-flagging breakpoint: tfcrop autoflag + flagmanager backup + plotms check + accept/revert.
- Baseline calibration (blcal): opt-in breakpoint, flux-gated, DR/flux-guarded.
- Results folder per run: FITS (exportfits), pbcor.tt0, PNG, clean mask, listobs, casa.log.
- Replay: call_recorder emits a standalone replay.py of the exact CASA calls (provenance
  header; tclean rewritten to reuse the saved mask non-interactively).
- Clean-mask save + replay through import.json, carried across cycles, with an --import prompt.
- Fixes: manual_self_cal breakpoint routing, array-config index, LAS C-band typo (8.9),
  Delos reachability pre-check (fail fast instead of a silent curl-retry hang).
